= Müsavat Reformation

Leaders of the German Democratic Party, seeing the party's vote share fall over time, has decided that now is the time to completely reform the party. The party leader, Erich Koch-Weser, has engineered a merger with the political arm of the Young German Order, a nationalist paramilitary group. Now, the party will be called the German State Party, or DStP.

This has led to outcry from the left wing of the party, progressives who would rather not work with antisemites and conservative nationalists.

- @advantage: We can recruit disaffected progressives to the RSDRP.
- @nothing: This is none of our concern.

@advantage
on-arrival: new_middle_rsdrp += 5; peoples_party_support += 1; left_dissent += 5; reformist_strength += 3; neorevisionist_strength += 3; reformist_dissent -= 2; neorevisionist_dissent -= 2

With turmoil in the Müsavat, we have an opportunity to recruit middle-class progressives and portions of the liberal intelligensia into our party. The left of the RSDRP is opposed to this path, seeing it as diluting the class character of the party. On the other hand, revisionists support this course.


@nothing

The Müsavat's internal affairs are none of our concern.